# Windows containment launchers are assembled from a template plus shared fragments and are then
# written to disk and executed by powershell.exe. Their end-of-line convention is pinned so the
# assembled launcher is identical on every checkout, and so the byte-for-byte golden comparison in
# WindowsContainmentScriptTest compares the same bytes on Linux and Windows agents.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.ps1frag text eol=crlf
*.ps1.template text eol=crlf
